      "writtenOn": "2015-07-07T23:10:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ah, I think what he\u0027s saying is that the temperature is encoded in the value so T \u003d 20 + value * 60 / 0x7fff.\n\nBut yes, it\u0027d be nicer to do the conversion in the EC so this is just degrees; that\u0027s more likely to be portable to other sensors.  Most temp sensors are only accurate to within a degree anyway.  And then define a constant for the unknown value:\n\n#define MOTIONSENSOR_CAL_TEMP_UNKNOWN 0x8000\n\n(or 0x80, if you use int8_t for temperature)",
